{:edb/db-before-t 1417 :edb/db-after-t 1418 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534730 50 #inst "2026-10-12T09:38:18.997Z" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186144526 1078 #edb/ref 17592186144528 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186144530 1078 #edb/ref 17592186144533 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186144544 1078 #edb/ref 17592186144547 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186144549 1078 #edb/ref 17592186144551 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186144560 1078 #edb/ref 17592186144562 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186147543 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434387 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186147544 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434388 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186147797 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186147797 1071 "Select the options that make the statement below true.\n\n$20%$ is equivalent to\n{{field-1}},\nwhich is\n{{field-2}}\n$\\frac{2}{5}$." 13194139534730 17592186045417 false] [17592186147797 1071 "Select the options that make the statement below true.\n\n$\\,$\n$20%$ is equivalent to \n{{field-1}},\nwhich is \n{{field-2}}\n$\\frac{2}{5}.$" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186147797 1074 "To convert the percent to a fraction, we first write $20%$ as a fraction with a denominator $100:$\n\n$$\n20%=\\frac{20}{100}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the fraction by dividing the numerator and denominator by $10:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{100}=\\frac{20÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{2}{10}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{10}=\\frac{2÷2}{10÷2}=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}<\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $20%$ is equivalent to $\\frac{1}{5},$ \nwhich is $\\text{smaller than}$ $\\frac{2}{5}.$" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186147799 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186147799 1071 "Matt and Abraham have the same number of marbles. A total of $63%$ of Matt's marbles are blue, while $\\frac{3}{4}$ of Abraham's marbles are blue. Select the options that make the statements below true.\n\n$\\,$\nA total of \n{{field-1}}\nof Abraham's marbles are blue. \n\n$\\,$\nTherefore, he has \n{{field-2}}\nblue marbles compared to Matt." 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186147799 1071 "Matt and Abraham have the same number of marbles. A total of $63%$ of Matt's marbles are blue, while $\\frac{3}{4}$ of Abraham's marbles are blue. Select the options that make the statements below true.\n\nA total of\n{{field-1}}\nof Abraham's marbles are blue.\n\nTherefore, he has\n{{field-2}}\nblue marbles compared to Matt." 13194139534730 17592186045417 false] [17592186147799 1074 "We need to compare $\\frac{3}{4}$ with $63%.$ We can do this by writing $\\frac{3}{4}$ as a percent.\n\nFirst, we write $\\frac{3}{4}$ as an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{3\\times 25}{4\\times 25}=\\frac{75}{100}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{75}{100}=75%\n$$\n\nSince $75%>63%,$ we have the following:\n\n- A total of $75%$ of Abraham's marbles are blue.\n\n- Therefore, he has $\\text{more}$ blue marbles compared to Matt." 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186147801 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186147801 1071 "Lionel and David are youth soccer players. In the previous season, $12%$ of Lionel’s goals were scored from the penalty spot, while the decimal proportion of David’s goals scored from the penalty spot was $0.1$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. Less than half of Lionel's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n2. More than half of David's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n3. Lionel had a greater percentage of goals scored from the penalty spot compared to David." 13194139534730 17592186045417 false] [17592186147801 1071 "Lionel and David are youth soccer players. In the previous season, $12%$ of Lionel’s goals were scored from the penalty spot, while the decimal proportion of David’s goals scored from the penalty spot was $0.1.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Less than half of Lionel's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n\nII. More than half of David's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n\nIII. Lionel had a greater percentage of goals scored from the penalty spot compared to David." 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186147801 1074 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n12%<50%,\n$$\n\nless than half of Lionel's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n0.1<0.5.\n$$\n\nSo, less than half of David's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n\n- Statement III is true. We can compare $12%$ and $0.1$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.1\\times 100=10%\n$$\n\nSince  $12%>10%,$ Lionel had a **greater** percentage of goals scored from the penalty spot compared to David.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434371 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434389 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434371 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434390 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434371 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434391 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434371 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434392 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434371 1043 #edb/ref 17592186434393 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434371 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434371 1045 "Comparing Fractions, Percents, and Decimals" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434371 1046 #edb/ref 17592186434389 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434371 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046648 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434371 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049531 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434371