82 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434385 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434383 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434385 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434385 1077 "field-2" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434385 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434382 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434385 1079 #uuid "0b435f79-e45f-54bc-a9c1-2ebc68f39df2" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434386 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434373 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434386 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434374 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434386 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434375 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434386 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434376 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434386 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434386 1077 "field-1" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434386 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434375 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434386 1079 #uuid "c1896846-f13a-5c11-a37a-ffc9a894ca42" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434387 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434385 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434387 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434386 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434387 1069 "q-349678" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434387 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434387 1071 "Select the options that make the statement below true.\n\n$\\,$\n$45%$ is equivalent to \n{{field-1}},\nwhich is \n{{field-2}}\n$\\frac{17}{40}.$" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434387 1072 #uuid "138791bc-5cad-58ca-ae3d-64015f9ea134" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434387 1074 "To convert the percent to a fraction, we first write $45%$ as a fraction with a denominator $100:$\n\n$$\n45%=\\frac{45}{100}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the fraction by dividing the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{45}{100}=\\frac{45÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{9}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can write this with a denominator of $40$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{20}=\\frac{9\\times 2}{20\\times 2}=\\frac{18}{40}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{18}{40}>\\frac{17}{40}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $45%$ is equivalent to $\\frac{18}{40},$ \nwhich is $\\text{greater than}$ $\\frac{17}{40}.$" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434388 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434384 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434388 1069 "q-350266" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434388 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434388 1071 "Sana and Talia are students. In the previous semester, the decimal proportion of Sana’s homework assignments that were turned in early was $0.4,$ while $45%$ of Talia’s homework assignments were turned in early. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Less than half of Sana's homework assignments were turned in early.\n\nII. More than half of Talia's homework assignments were turned in early.\n\nIII. Sana had a greater percentage of homework assignments turned in early compared to Talia." 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434388 1072 #uuid "16a4ed86-6ba4-5b08-b5bc-00c64da3da49" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434388 1074 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n0.4<0.5,\n$$\n\nless than half of Sana's homework assignments were turned in early.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n45%<50%.\n$$\n\nSo, less than half of Talia's homework assignments were turned in early.\n\n- Statement III is false. We can compare $0.4$ and $45%$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.4\\times 100=40%\n$$\n\nSince  $40%<45%,$ Sana did not have a greater percentage of homework assignments turned in early compared to Talia.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434389 1058 #edb/ref 17592186434392 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434389 1062 #uuid "334dd9af-1647-5c57-bfb3-97a4e3ad59e7" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434389 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147797 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434390 1058 #edb/ref 17592186434391 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434390 1062 #uuid "37767ed4-b4c6-547e-a639-f6aeaee3ddec" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434390 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147801 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434391 1058 #edb/ref 17592186434393 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434391 1062 #uuid "63533d39-a10e-52e0-8ad1-5274656cd410" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434391 1063 #edb/ref 17592186434387 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434392 1058 #edb/ref 17592186434390 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434392 1062 #uuid "cf9b1dbf-2308-5acb-ba12-635c8825ef8b" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434392 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147799 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434393 1062 #uuid "e00df753-1591-526d-a3e8-f3c5207c5bfd" 13194139534730 17592186045417 true] [17592186434393 1063 #edb/ref 17592186434388 13194139534730 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-8fdc0e2d-e98a-546b-920a-d66ad029459e" 17592186434371 "answer-1129c1e9-1f22-5780-9696-b4a255e78851" 17592186434372 "answer-355f6139-1632-5fb9-a099-f60c0204143d" 17592186434373 "answer-43eb7fb9-45e1-5182-81e4-f59709d8a423" 17592186434374 "answer-4da1f349-69e6-5209-8396-1c722ffbf3d6" 17592186434375 "answer-4e451e41-9d76-5570-9fd1-85be78bfe38d" 17592186434376 "answer-585c654e-1a6c-5f56-ac8d-5f161ee40bff" 17592186434377 "answer-6fc398c3-ef25-52ba-8a15-a914c2acb08b" 17592186434378 "answer-739f06d6-c702-56c9-a051-08e032332d7a" 17592186434379 "answer-9ab8acb2-0f16-5f40-8fd6-1f3209f135e3" 17592186434380 "answer-c956c11a-2fd4-59e8-a085-706468c3a376" 17592186434381 "answer-cb6ea343-a5aa-5d69-b351-d0c27cab6e7f" 17592186434382 "answer-f5